# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Production only — the Docker/nginx tester
# preview ignores this file and gets the same set from config/nginx.conf.
# Change one, change the other.
#
# Astro emits the real Content-Security-Policy as a per-page <meta http-equiv>,
# because every script on this site is inlined into the document and only the
# build knows their hashes (see security.csp in astro.config.mjs). The CSP below
# carries just frame-ancestors, which a <meta> CSP cannot express — browsers
# ignore it there. Two policies on one page are both enforced, so this adds the
# framing rule rather than replacing the generated one.

# HSTS carries no includeSubDomains and no preload: myridesg.com has siblings
# this repo does not own, and preload is a one-way door. Widen it deliberately.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Hashed filenames, so they can never go stale.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json
